  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Alliance for TB Drug Development II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  .With assistance from USAID, the TB Alliance will link the best practices and drives of the private sector with the health equity priorities and resources of the public sector. This process helps design new ways to leverage worldwide science and market forces for public good. Anticipated developments include: introduction of at least one moxifloxacin-based new treatment-shortening regimen; movement of a MDR-TB treatment through Phase III trials; and development of treatments for drug-resistant TB and drug-sensitive TB...Global Health Bureau will continue to accelerate activities to address multi-drug resistant (MDR) and extensively drug resistant tuberculosis, including the expansion of diagnosis and treatment, and infection control measures through innovative MDR financing mechanisms... .</narrative>
  </description>
